From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Erik Berg <fedora@slipsprogrammor.no>
Date: Wed, 9 Sep 2026 21:22:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] UefiCpuPkg/CpuDxe: don't assert in memory attribute protocol
 on non-PAE IA32

Windows' 32-bit boot loader (BOOTIA32.EFI) calls the EFI Memory
Attribute Protocol with paging disabled right after loading cdboot.efi.
CpuDxe's GetCurrentPagingContext reads CR0/CR4 live on every protocol
call, and EfiGetMemoryAttributes had no non-PAE guard: it walked into
GetPageTableEntry and hit ASSERT CpuPageTable.c(336) -> CpuDeadLoop.

Return EFI_UNSUPPORTED from EfiGetMemoryAttributes when the live
context is IA32 non-PAE or paging-off (Set/Clear were already guarded
via ConvertMemoryPageAttributes), and skip installing the protocol
entirely when the context at driver start cannot support it.

Verified on qemu q35+kvm with a Windows 10 x86 ISO: unpatched firmware
from the same tree reproduces the assert, patched firmware boots to
the Windows Setup language dialog.
---
 UefiCpuPkg/CpuDxe/CpuPageTable.c | 31 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 30 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/UefiCpuPkg/CpuDxe/CpuPageTable.c b/UefiCpuPkg/CpuDxe/CpuPageTable.c
index 4171c247b8..0393610b9f 100644
--- a/UefiCpuPkg/CpuDxe/CpuPageTable.c
+++ b/UefiCpuPkg/CpuDxe/CpuPageTable.c
@@ -1667,6 +1667,17 @@ EfiGetMemoryAttributes (
 
   GetCurrentPagingContext (&CurrentPagingContext);
 
+  //
+  // Page table walking below requires PAE format entries; without paging or
+  // with 32-bit non-PAE paging there is nothing this protocol can report.
+  //
+  if ((CurrentPagingContext.MachineType == IMAGE_FILE_MACHINE_I386) &&
+      (((CurrentPagingContext.ContextData.Ia32.Attributes & PAGE_TABLE_LIB_PAGING_CONTEXT_IA32_X64_ATTRIBUTES_PAE) == 0) ||
+       (CurrentPagingContext.ContextData.Ia32.PageTableBase == 0)))
+  {
+    return EFI_UNSUPPORTED;
+  }
+
   do {
     PageEntry = GetPageTableEntry (&CurrentPagingContext, BaseAddress, &PageAttr);
     if ((PageEntry == NULL) || (PageAttr == PageNone)) {
@@ -1730,7 +1741,25 @@ InstallEfiMemoryAttributeProtocol (
   IN EFI_HANDLE  Handle
   )
 {
-  EFI_STATUS  Status;
+  EFI_STATUS                     Status;
+  PAGE_TABLE_LIB_PAGING_CONTEXT  CurrentPagingContext;
+
+  GetCurrentPagingContext (&CurrentPagingContext);
+
+  //
+  // The protocol cannot manage page attributes when the CPU runs without
+  // paging or with 32-bit non-PAE paging (no NX support, 32-bit entries),
+  // so do not advertise it in those environments. Consumers such as the
+  // Windows boot manager treat a present-but-failing implementation as
+  // fatal, while coping fine with the protocol being absent.
+  //
+  if ((CurrentPagingContext.MachineType == IMAGE_FILE_MACHINE_I386) &&
+      (((CurrentPagingContext.ContextData.Ia32.Attributes & PAGE_TABLE_LIB_PAGING_CONTEXT_IA32_X64_ATTRIBUTES_PAE) == 0) ||
+       (CurrentPagingContext.ContextData.Ia32.PageTableBase == 0)))
+  {
+    DEBUG ((DEBUG_INFO, "%a: no PAE paging, skipping installation\n", __func__));
+    return;
+  }
 
   Status = gBS->InstallMultipleProtocolInterfaces (
                   &Handle,
-- 
2.51.0
